  "worked_solution": "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{4-3x}-2 & \\le 0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{4-3x} & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{4-3x})}^{3} & \\le {2}^{3} \\\\ 4-3x & \\le 8 \\\\ -3x & \\le 4 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that, in the last step, we had to flip the sign of the inequality because we divided by a negative number.\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -\\frac{4}{3}.$",
